# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Consumer setup for @al-rayhaanat/*
#
# Copy this file to `.npmrc` in the ROOT of the project that will install the
# design system. It tells your package manager that anything scoped
# `@al-rayhaanat` lives on GitHub Packages, not the public npm registry.
#
#   cp .npmrc.example .npmrc
#
# `.npmrc` is gitignored on purpose — never commit a token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@al-rayhaanat:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com

# Authentication.
#
# Reads the token from the GITHUB_TOKEN environment variable so the token
# itself never lands in a file. Export it from your shell profile
# (~/.zshrc on macOS):
#
#   export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# The token needs only the `read:packages` scope. Create one at:
#   https://github.com/settings/tokens/new?scopes=read:packages
#
# If your org enforces SSO, click "Configure SSO" on the token afterwards and
# authorise it for the al-rayhaanat organisation — otherwise every install
# fails with a 401 that does not mention SSO anywhere.
#
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
